# Goal: print the current ARP/IPv6-neighbour table in the standard readable form.
# Input: kernel neighbour state, queried through `ip`.
# Change: none; this is a read-only observation.
# Boundary: a missing neighbour does not prove that the host is unreachable.
# Role of yesh: make the read-only network check and failure path explicit; Linux networking tools provide the observation.

ip neigh show
